# Contributing

Use Go 1.27.3, Task v3.53.1 and GOWORK=off. This application owns its generated
source; normal builds do not depend on the CLI checkout. Do not add sibling replaces.

Install Task and the check tools outside this module and put their binaries on PATH:

```sh
go install github.com/go-task/task/v3/cmd/task@v3.53.1
go install github.com/golangci/golangci-lint/v2/cmd/golangci-lint@v2.15.0
go install golang.org/x/vuln/cmd/govulncheck@v1.9.0
```

```sh
go mod download
task check INTEGRATION=true
task lint
task vulncheck
[[if .GRPC]]task api[[end]]
```

Checks force GOWORK=off. GO, GOFMT, GOLANGCI_LINT and GOVULNCHECK select executable
paths, including spaces. fmt, fix and tidy intentionally apply changes.
Only check, test, build, lint, vulncheck, fmt, fix and tidy are public general
tasks. Bare task selects check. Use test RACE=true, COVER=true or INTEGRATION=true
for race detection, coverage or integration tests. Coverage includes race detection. Check reuses race-enabled test
and forwards the integration option; CI explicitly enables it.
[[if .GRPC]]The additional api task selects generate, lint, check or breaking with
ACTION; its default check does not change generated output.[[end]]

Native HTTP APIs need no Proto generation. Review request/response fields, implement
identity, authorization and application calls, and explicitly mount each handler.
No placeholder tests are generated; write behavior tests for implemented operations.
[[if .GRPC]]
Proto contracts require Buf 1.72.0. Contract tasks call the pinned CLI, which downloads
pinned Go plugins; no system protoc is needed. Use an absolute NOSTOSX executable
path for source builds or NOSTOSX_VERSION for a reviewed release.
After changing Proto or HTTP mapping, run task api ACTION=generate, go mod tidy and task api.
Select gateway runtime v2.29.0 explicitly when first using gateway bindings. Pure gRPC
needs no gateway runtime. Never edit generated Go/OpenAPI output. Compatibility checks
require an explicit versioned Git baseline. All operations honor .nostosx.lock; plugin
failures preserve old output and ordinary publication errors attempt rollback.
[[end]]
Keep domain/application independent of transport types. Place consumer-owned ports
beside actual use cases and service-private adapters under services/<name>/internal.
Construct dependencies explicitly in app.go; introduce CQRS/middleware only when
actual behavior needs it. Do not add fake APIs, database scaffolds or architecture tests.

Use integration-tagged tests for listeners and model fixtures. Exercise cancellation,
authorization and cleanup using temporary resources, without operator credentials or
shared stores. Go tests must join their goroutines before completion.

Template upgrades do not automatically rewrite this application. Review source changes
and update behavior tests. Publication and deployment require explicit authorization.
